==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|enm|straungely|t=strangely, aloofly, intricately}}; equivalent to {{suffix|en|strange|ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈstɹeɪndʒli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-strangely.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[strange]] or [[coincidental]] manner.
# {{lb|en|archaic}} Surprisingly, wonderfully.
#* '''1610''', ''[[s:The Tempest|The Tempest]]'', by [[w:William Shakespeare|Shakespeare]], act 4 scene 1
#*: [...] all thy vexations / Were but my trials of thy love, and thou / Hast '''strangely''' stood the test [...]

